{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaExponentKeystone","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaExponentKeystone","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":21,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.mirror_baseline_cancels","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.mirror_baseline_cancels","kind":"theorem","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaExponentKeystone.lean#L247-L265","doc":"**The mirror cancellation (proved; the separation is the hypothesis).** Model\nthe Δ_λ deviation as `f Z N = baseline (Z+N) + zCorr (Z − N)` — an A-only\nbaseline plus a term in the interface imbalance `Z − N`, the additive form\njustified by the mirror-invariance of the two bar-even statistics above. Then\nthe mirror-pair difference cancels the baseline **exactly** (since\n`Z + N = N + Z`) and equals `zCorr (Z−N) − zCorr (N−Z)`: the observable mirror\nsplit is the bar-odd Z-correction alone, independent of the (A-dependent,\ncollapsing) baseline.\n\nThe cancellation given the additive form is *unconditional*; the separation\nhypothesis `hf` itself is the additive-channel ansatz (supplied, not proved —\nthe data confirms it but the corpus gates fitting its magnitude). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:mirror-baseline-cancellation","label":"prop:mirror-baseline-cancellation","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-mass-binding-algorithms/mba-sidecar-mirror-cancellation.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.atomWrithe_mirror_difference","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.atomWrithe_mirror_difference","kind":"theorem","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaExponentKeystone.lean#L237-L245","doc":"**Derived.** The atomWrithe is *not* mirror-invariant: it maps `4Z ↦ 4N`, and\nthe mirror difference is `4(Z − N)`. The atomWrithe is therefore the **unique**\ncrossing statistic that distinguishes a mirror pair — the entire mirror-pair\ndifference is carried by the bar-odd channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.averaged_count_mirror_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.averaged_count_mirror_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaExponentKeystone.lean#L232-L235","doc":"**Derived.** The color-averaged count `2A + 1` is also mirror-invariant —\nthe second bar-even statistic is A-only too. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.crossing_sum_mirror_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.crossing_sum_mirror_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaExponentKeystone.lean#L225-L230","doc":"**Derived.** The crossing sum is invariant under the mirror swap `Z ↔ N`\n(it is A-only): the bar-even leading content is identical across a mirror pair. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.he3_penalised_more_than_triton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.he3_penalised_more_than_triton","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaExponentKeystone.lean#L204-L211","doc":"**Conditional (proved; the asymmetry is the hypothesis).** *If* the\nproton-excess penalty asymmetry holds, then proton-rich ³He (`Z−N = +1`) has a\nstrictly larger binding-exponent deficit than its mirror triton (`Z−N = −1`) —\nthe `−1.40` vs `−0.07` outlier pattern. Asserts nothing about whether the\nhypothesis holds; only the structural consequence at `k = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ProtonExcessPenaltyAsymmetry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ProtonExcessPenaltyAsymmetry","kind":"def","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaExponentKeystone.lean#L186-L202","doc":"**Conjectural bridge (NOT asserted).** The structural asymmetry the binding\ndata exhibits on mirror pairs: writing `δ` for the measured Δ_λ q₀-exponent\ndeviation indexed by the interface imbalance `Z−N`, the proton-rich member\n(`Z−N = +k`, `k>0`) is penalised strictly more than its neutron-rich mirror\n(`Z−N = −k`).\n\nThis is a content-bearing *conjecture predicate* — its truth is the OPEN claim,\ndeliberately NOT asserted (Δ_λ gate: the coefficient `≈ −1.4` per excess proton\nis measured, never fitted into the closure). It is the honest Z-companion to\n`perSiteFiveClaim`: derived arithmetic (`atomWrithe = 4Z`; the p≠n seed `3 ≠ 1`)\nfeeds a named-but-unproved bridge to the observable. Stated over any `Preorder`\nso it makes no archimedean commitment beyond the order on the deviations.\n\n  -- Ref: [leitner2026] docs/audits/2026-06-29-delta-lambda-z-correction-atomWrithe.md\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.atomWrithe_intra_interface_decomp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.atomWrithe_intra_interface_decomp","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaExponentKeystone.lean#L176-L184","doc":"**Derived.** The atomWrithe splits as `intra (3Z+N) + interface (Z−N) = 4Z`,\nreconciling `atomWrithe_eq_four_Z` with the per-nucleon seeds and the interface\nimbalance. The intra term is the *defined* `intraWrithe` (cast to `ℤ`); the\ninterface term is signed, hence the identity lives over `ℤ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.interfaceImbalance_eq_Z_sub_N","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.interfaceImbalance_eq_Z_sub_N","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaExponentKeystone.lean#L168-L174","doc":"**Derived.** The interface imbalance equals `Z − N`. This is the\n*mirror-pair splitter*: the only atomWrithe contribution that distinguishes ³He\n(`Z−N = +1`) from the triton T (`Z−N = −1`) — the two share `σ+σ⁻¹ = 28`, hence\nan identical leading exponent `25`, and differ only here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.interfaceImbalance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.interfaceImbalance","kind":"def","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaExponentKeystone.lean#L163-L166","doc":"The interface chirality imbalance `(Z−1) − (N−1)`: each `p-p` interface is a\n`σ` (+1), each `n-n` a `σ⁻¹` (−1), the single `p-n` is bar-symmetric (0). Signed,\nhence stated over `ℤ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.intraWrithe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.intraWrithe","kind":"def","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaExponentKeystone.lean#L160-L161","doc":"Total intra atomWrithe of the atom: the per-nucleon seeds summed, `3Z + N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.proton_neutron_intra_writhe_asymmetry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.proton_neutron_intra_writhe_asymmetry","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaExponentKeystone.lean#L152-L158","doc":"**The p≠n seed (derived).** A proton and a neutron carry *different* intra\natomWrithe (`3 ≠ 1`): the proton walk is more positive-chirality. This inequality\nis the structural origin of the asymmetric proton-excess penalty — why ³He\n(one excess proton) is penalised sharply while its mirror T (one excess\nneutron) is barely touched. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.neutronIntraWrithe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.neutronIntraWrithe","kind":"def","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaExponentKeystone.lean#L149-L150","doc":"Per-nucleon intra-𝓑₃ atomWrithe of a neutron walk: `5σ − 4σ⁻¹ = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.protonIntraWrithe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.protonIntraWrithe","kind":"def","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaExponentKeystone.lean#L146-L147","doc":"Per-nucleon intra-𝓑₃ atomWrithe of a proton walk: `6σ − 3σ⁻¹ = 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.atomWrithe_eq_four_Z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.atomWrithe_eq_four_Z","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaExponentKeystone.lean#L136-L144","doc":"**Derived.** The atomWrithe is `4Z`: the `A`/`N` content cancels, leaving\n*proton number only*. This is the bar-ANTISYMMETRIC (q ↦ q⁻¹–odd) companion to\n`crossing_sum_cancels`. The symmetric sum `σ+σ⁻¹ = 10A−2` is A-only and sets\nthe leading exponent `10A−5`; the antisymmetric atomWrithe `σ−σ⁻¹ = 4Z` is Z-only\nand is the *source* of the proton-excess correction the data demands (³He). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.atomWrithe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.atomWrithe","kind":"def","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaExponentKeystone.lean#L127-L134","doc":"Writhe (signed crossing total) of the atom braid word: `σ − σ⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.perSiteFive_of_exponent_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.perSiteFive_of_exponent_eq","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaExponentKeystone.lean#L84-L114","doc":"**Conditional restatement (proved; the conjectural content is the\nhypothesis).** *If* the Δ_λ binding exponent equals `10A − 5`, then the\nper-site-`5` claim `perSiteFiveClaim` holds — this direction is the pure\narithmetic factorization. The file asserts nothing about whether the\nhypothesis `hexp` is true.\n\n⚠ The hypothesis `hexp` (binding exponent = `10A − 5`, i.e. `5` per chain-\nsite) is exactly the OPEN, magnitude-contested claim — it is supplied here,\nnot proved. Two layers of doubt:\n1. *Underived.* Why each chain-site contributes exactly `5` (the Bring\n   quintic degree) is not derived from the jet order (Step 8) or the\n   Gröbner–Shirshov normal form (Step 7); the crossing count merely asserts\n   it.\n2. *Empirically contested.* Per `2026-06-15-delta-lambda-q5-per-site-\n   mechanism-start.md`, the literal `q₀^{5(2A−1)}` exponent overpredicts the\n   measured `B_sym/B_lin` ratio by 3×→145×; the fitted exponent is ≈ 1.4 per\n   site, consistent with an exp-vs-linear (Kashaev) correction, not a\n   `q₀`-power.\n\nThe honest next step is to measure the per-site exponent from real compute\nbefore chasing the complex-q mechanism for \"why 5\". Keeping the contested\nclaim as a *hypothesis* (rather than a `sorry`-conjecture asserting it) avoids\nenshrining a refuted near-match while still recording the precise statement.\n\n  -- Ref: [leitner2026] docs/audits/2026-06-19-delta-lambda-exponent-keystone-formalize-first.md\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.perSiteFiveClaim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.perSiteFiveClaim","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaExponentKeystone.lean#L77-L82","doc":"The contested bridge claim, as a precise predicate (not asserted true):\nthe Δ_λ binding `q₀`-exponent for an isotope with `A` nucleons equals\n`5·(2A − 1)` — i.e. exactly `5` per chain-site. Stated so the conjecture\nbelow has a name; the truth value is open. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.exponent_factorization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.exponent_factorization","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaExponentKeystone.lean#L69-L75","doc":"**Derived (pure arithmetic).** The per-site factorization: `10A − 5`\nfactors as `5·(2A − 1) = 5 × (A nucleon-sites + (A−1) bond-sites)`. This is\nthe arithmetic *shape* of the asserted per-site reading; it does not assert\nthat the binding exponent equals it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.crossing_sum_cancels","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.crossing_sum_cancels","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaExponentKeystone.lean#L60-L67","doc":"**Derived.** The proton and neutron crossing counts sum to `10A − 2`\n(`A = Z + N`): the `Z`/`N` coefficients cancel, giving the slope of 10\ncrossings per nucleon. Requires at least one nucleon (`1 ≤ Z + N`) so the\ntruncated `ℕ` subtractions are exact. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.neutronCrossings","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.neutronCrossings","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaExponentKeystone.lean#L57-L58","doc":"Negative (neutron-interface) crossings in the atom braid word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.protonCrossings","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.protonCrossings","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaExponentKeystone.lean#L53-L55","doc":"Positive (proton-walk) crossings in the atom braid word for `Z` protons,\n`N` neutrons. Closed form from `atom_braid_word_3A`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}